problem: A lot people hate history or don't even know about their civilization so we will develop an educational game about history so they can like history again 
targeted people: Anyone who hates history or wishes to experience the life back in time


GENERAL IDEA OF THE PROJECT:
We will develop a game that evolves around history where we simulate the events of historical centuries like ancient Egypt and the American revolution. 
And the player will witness these events in our game as they will be playing as a citizen for instance or as a king after leveling up (will discuss levels with details later on).
There will be also a leveling system which will be the motivation to play as by leveling up you can: experience more historical events , unlocking cosmetics to design your avatar or replaying some events but with different roles.
We will also feature some quizzes and questions to test the player's knowledge which will be in the form of "side quests".
There will be some boss fights to also fulfill the gaming side alongside the educational side.
And finally, a multiplayer mode where players from varies parts of the world will put their historical knowledge and gaming skill to the ultimate test.



GAMEPLAY:
You play as simple citizen in a civilization where you will basically live there.
You will experience the kings' rulings , the economical state of the civilization , will witness the fall of civilization or participate on rising a new one.
You can witness the construction of the great pyramids or even participate in the French and Indian war and so on.
As the player proceeds deep enough in the events they will gain XP to level up and that's where our second subject begins...


LEVEL UP SYSTEM
By playing the game , gaining enough XP and testing the player's knowledge , They can level up. The benefits of leveling up are as following:
1- Unlocking more historical events to try
2- Unlocking cool cosmetics to design your avatar
3- Unlocking weapons to use in multiplayer or side quests 

But how do we level up? Simple by playing and completing side quests.
Side quests will play a huge role in the game as it's the only way to grind for XP (After playing he game ofc).
Side quests mostly will evolve around answering some questions or taking quizzes to test one's historical knowledge. 
Or it can be a boss fight or doings some certain actions in order to complete the side quest in question.



MULTIPLAYER:
Multiplayer will serve two sides: Educational and Gaming sides

Educational side:
Will evolve on players competing against each other on who solves the questions or quizzes faster and most importantly correctly.
Playing their will reward the player with XP , cosmetics and weapons that can't be claimed by any means other than the mentioned method.
There where also a global leaderboard to add some spice to the competition. Playing this side will be unlimited (No energy needed to participate).

GAMING side:
Unlike the educational side , energy is required to participate in this side.
Here it will be a 1v1 duels featuring each two players' avatars as warriors and are using weapons claimed from leveling up.
The ONLY way to obtain energy to participate is only by testing your historical knowledge in the EDUCATIONAL side. 
There will also be a global leaderboard here too to add some heat.
So basically it's just two noble warriors fighting till death claim ONE of their souls.
